<body>
    <h1>Trade Allocations Monitor</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrappe=
r confluence-embedded-manual-size"><a href=3D"https://purplegroup3.atlassia=
n.net/wiki/download/attachments/3075866628/Trade%20Monitor%20Technical%20Fi=
nal.mp4?version=3D2&amp;modificationDate=3D1696324652715&amp;cacheVersion=
=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2">Trade Monitor Technical Final.mp4</a></span>
<p></p>
<style type=3D"text/css">/*<![CDATA[*/
div.rbtoc1759150270744 {padding: 0px;}
div.rbtoc1759150270744 ul {list-style: disc;margin-left: 0px;}
div.rbtoc1759150270744 li {margin-left: 0px;padding-left: 0px;}

/*]]>*/</style>
<div class=3D"toc-macro rbtoc1759150270744">
<ul class=3D"toc-indentation">
<li><a href=3D"#TradeAllocationsMonitor-TradeAllocations:">TradeAllocations=
:</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"#TradeAllocationsMonitor-TradeAllocationsAPI:">Trade Allocat=
ions API:</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"#TradeAllocationsMonitor-TradeMonitor:">Trade Monitor:</a>
<ul class=3D"toc-indentation">
<li><a href=3D"#TradeAllocationsMonitor-TradeRequestMonitorAggregatorMessag=
e:">TradeRequestMonitorAggregatorMessage:</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"#TradeAllocationsMonitor-TradeGroupStatus:">TradeGroupStatus=
:</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"#TradeAllocationsMonitor-Aggregatorlogic:">Aggregator logic:=
</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"#TradeAllocationsMonitor-processTradeallocationGroupComplete=
:">processTradeallocationGroupComplete:</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"#TradeAllocationsMonitor-GETmethods:">GET methods:</a></li>
</ul></li>
<li><a href=3D"#TradeAllocationsMonitor-Testing,capacityplanning:">Testing,=
 capacity planning:</a></li>
</ul>
</div>
<hr>
<p>The purpose of this application is to monitor groups of trades placed in=
 bulk via the Trade Allocations services, and on completion of the last tra=
de in the group, notify other applications via Kafka events.</p>
<p>The <strong>Trade Group Monitor</strong> service itself is an additional=
 service with a Mongo database that saves Trade monitor Kafka messages, wit=
h APIs to query the status by group or individual trade allocationid, useri=
d, trustaccountid, or transactionid. This can be used by other systems like=
 Admin to check the status of a user=E2=80=99s trades without having to que=
ry the Trade allocations table. The Trade allocations database table has to=
 manage trade requests and should not be available long term. The intention=
 was always to delete successful or error status trades and only keep unall=
ocated requests in the database until they finish processing.</p>
<p>Trade Monitor saves all the trade monitor request messages with the same=
 data as found in the TradeAllocations table. As the trade monitor sends up=
dated states, the Trade Monitor services will update the allocation status =
and data via its consumer.</p>
<p>These trades will be saved into a MongoDB and APIs will be created to qu=
ery the status of a group of trades.</p>
<p><strong>TradeMonitor</strong> - Trade Requests table in Mongo has the da=
ta as below.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: csharp; gutter: false; theme: Django" data-theme=3D"Django">create table =
dbo.TradeAllocation
(
    TradeAllocationId          bigint identity
    UserId                     bigint,
    InstrumentId               bigint,
    Price                      float,
    TrustAccountId             bigint,
    Amount                     decimal(20, 4),
    Units                      decimal(25, 15),
    TradeTypeID                int,
    AllocationStatusId         int
    TransactionID              bigint,
    TrustAccountActionId       bigint,
    FailureReason              varchar(max),
    GroupId                    uniqueidentifier,
    DepositRequired            bit,
    CostCalculationType        int,
    UniqueTransactionReference varchar(50),
    DateCreated                datetime,
    TriggerOnDate              datetime,
    TransactionTag             varchar(100) default NULL,
    IsCashMovement             bit          default 0,
    AllowNegativeMovement      bit,
    TraderID                   bigint,
    TotalTradeRequestsInGroup  int</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Additional work was done on Trade Allocations Applications:</p>
<h3 id=3D"TradeAllocationsMonitor-TradeAllocations:"><strong>TradeAllocatio=
ns</strong>:</h3>
<p>The Trade Allocations service sends out a Kafka message called TradeMoni=
torMessage with the following schema to the <strong>trade_allocation_status=
_update_monitor</strong> Kafka topic:</p>
<p class=3D"media-group"><img height=3D"250" style=3D"margin: 2px; border: =
1px solid #ddd; box-sizing: border-box; vertical-align: text-bottom;" src=
=3D"d14924ff7514894371c033bc38921aa1d169af949f7ae84d697afe3149c085b7" width=
=3D"250"></p>
<p>This will be done every time a trade allocation status is changed.</p>
<p>Trade Allocations Source table will be updated to read TotalTradeRequest=
sInGroup associated to a trade allocation</p>
<p>ALTER TABLE [GT247CFD].[dbo].[TradeAllocation]<br>
ADD TotalTradeRequestsInGroup INT NULL;</p>
<p>ADD <code>Proceeds double</code></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Update <code>ALLOCATION_TO_QUEUE_QUERY</code></p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<h3 id=3D"TradeAllocationsMonitor-TradeAllocationsAPI:"><strong>Trade Alloc=
ations API</strong>:</h3>
<p>On every allocation status change after a TradeAllocationEntity is updat=
ed, a TradeMonitorMessage (same as above) will be sent to the <strong>trade=
_allocation_status_update_monitor</strong> topic.</p>
<p>On client trade success message consumed in Trade Allocations API, units=
 and price are set before TradeAllocationsEntity is saved. Risk and Transac=
tionPrice can be found in the TradeDTO object in the client trade success k=
afka message already consumed.</p>
<p></p>
<p>NB Placing Trade Allocations Groups to be added for group tracking where=
 GroupID and total trades in group is set <strong>programmatically</strong>=
.</p>
<p><strong> </strong></p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"TradeAllocationsMonitor-TradeMonitor:"><strong>Trade Monitor:</st=
rong></h3>
<p><strong>Kafka Stream aggregation to track allocations by group and notif=
y when the whole group is done: </strong></p>
<p>Trades are executed as a batch by using the TradeAllocations <code>group=
Id</code> column. When a managed product investment is done, it consists of=
 <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"ca55801b-1d5e-45fe-928c-=
6970e1cc57ff">multiple trades</span> that make up the investment according =
to the asset managers' specifications. E.g. Investing <span class=3D"inline=
-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"d48cb536-5335-476e-9932-628cca96ca76">$100</sp=
an> in a product may result in 5 trades being placed with different weighti=
ng into different instruments. These trades will be placed by putting the i=
nstructions into the TradeAllocations (bulk trading) application=E2=80=99s =
database via its apis. It currently has a group ID which can be used to sta=
rt the processing of the whole batch, as well as grouping trades together. =
We will be using this groupId to track trade execution and send out an even=
t when the whole group has completed. <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker"=
 data-ref=3D"bacd40b9-0e4e-4f50-ae58-7580efcd6d67">Completed means when all=
 trades was done</span>, including failures=E2=80=A6 ie. <span class=3D"inl=
ine-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"c7472f99-022d-40cb-8bcc-1a67c930307c">You c=
ould have a batch of 10 trades where 9 will pass and 1 failed</span> and th=
e Trade Monitor will send out an event to notify that it has completed.</p>
<p>Create a new table that keeps track of the whole group with api methods =
to query the status of a group.</p>
<p>This will be updated by the Aggregation message and if a Trade complete =
event is sent, all subsequent messages in the aggregator should be ignored.=
 We can add duplicate checks in the consumer to ensure we don=E2=80=99t pro=
cess a message twice. (Research on how to do this in Kafka streams methods =
and wether we can use our custom annotation should be done). This can happe=
n on messages being re-processed incorrectly and duplicate error occur that=
 will send error status updates.</p>
<p>In order to notify the rest of the business when a batch of trades, boun=
d together with the same GroupID in the TradeAllocations table, has complet=
ed, we will use the messages from the trade_request_monitor topic (<a href=
=3D"https://purplegroup3.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PG/pages/3030188057/Trad=
e+Allocations+-+New+Kafka+implementation" data-linked-resource-id=3D"303018=
8057" data-linked-resource-version=3D"20" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page=
">see Trade Allocations documentation</a>) and apply kafka stream aggregati=
on to them.</p>
<p>A new aggregated topic will be created called <strong>trade_allocation_g=
roup_complete. </strong></p>
<p>This topic will ingest TradeMonitorMessage events and create the followi=
ng <strong>KTABLE</strong>, aggregated by groupID.</p>
<h4 id=3D"TradeAllocationsMonitor-TradeRequestMonitorAggregatorMessage:"><s=
trong>TradeRequestMonitorAggregatorMessage:</strong></h4>
<p><strong>GroupID</strong>: GroupId of the TradeAllocation Instruction.</p=
>
<p><strong>TotalTradeRequestsInGroup</strong>: This field will be overwritt=
en every time since it will remain constant and always show what the expect=
ed total amount in the group should be.</p>
<p><strong>TotalSuccess</strong>: This field will be increased when a trade=
 monitor message is consumed and the following is true:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>If TradeTypeId =3D 1 (Trade), and<span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" d=
ata-ref=3D"da27b78c-1858-48f4-800a-5103cf8faf6f"> allocationStatusId =3D <s=
pan class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"55ef46ef-29b4-4767-a527-625=
66851cc2c">2</span></span></p></li>
<li>
<p>Or if allocationStatusId =3D 4. (Orders goes to 2, then they trigger whe=
n markets open and become successful trades, which is then marked as 4 in T=
rade allocations and the subsequents TradeRequestMonitor message</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>TotalFailed</strong>: This field increase by 1 every time a mess=
age is received that has allocationStatusId =3D 3, which indicated a failed=
 trade allocation.</p>
<p><strong>TradesInGroup</strong>: List of trade allocation entities with c=
urrent state. <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"7613c7f6-d6=
71-4c15-bb84-3fc7e4504789">If current entry exists in the List, replace wit=
h updated values of the current TradeMonitorMessage.</span></p>
<p><strong>TrustAccountID</strong></p>
<p>KTable events will be sent out on any changes, at a certain interval (co=
nfigured in application.properties usually 1 sec).</p>
<p>We need to save these updates by groupID to a new mongo table in order t=
o query easily.</p>
<p>Table data:</p>
<h4 id=3D"TradeAllocationsMonitor-TradeGroupStatus:"><strong>TradeGroupStat=
us:</strong></h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: csharp; gutter: false; theme: Django" data-theme=3D"Django">groupid (uuid=
)
totalSuccess (int),=20
totalFailed (int),=20
TotalTradesInGroup (int),=20
TotalProceeds(double),=20
OverallStatus (int),  (0 =3D incomplete, 1 =3D group successful, 2 =3D grou=
p complete with errors)</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"TradeAllocationsMonitor-Aggregatorlogic:"><strong><span class=3D"=
inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"1d14191d-a59b-4305-9a88-1ddc78e2c499">Ag=
gregator logic:</span> </strong></h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: csharp; gutter: false; theme: Django" data-theme=3D"Django">If tradeTypeI=
d =3D 1 (trade) and status =3D 2, totalSuccess++

If status =3D 3, totalFail++

If status =3D 4, totalSuccess++</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>The Aggregated KTable will at an interval of 1 second, if there were cha=
nges, send out the aggregated message containing the latest state of the gr=
oup to a new topic. E.g</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: csharp; gutter: false; theme: Django" data-theme=3D"Django">Message 1: { =
GroupId x, totalSuccess =3D 1, totalFailed =3D 2, totalTradeRequestInGroup =
=3D 10}

Message 2: { GroupId x, totalSuccess =3D 3, totalFailed =3D 3, totalTradeRe=
questInGroup =3D 10}

Message 3: { GroupId x, totalSuccess =3D 7, totalFailed =3D 3, totalTradeRe=
questInGroup =3D 10}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"3c058500-9ec3-4e40-bbe=
6-ea9069ef8d36">This topic will be consume again by TradeMonitor, and on ea=
ch message check the following: </span></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: csharp; gutter: false; theme: Django" data-theme=3D"Django">If (totalTrad=
eRequestInGroup =3D (totalFailed + totalSuccess){

  processTradeallocationGroupComplete(GroupId)

}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"TradeAllocationsMonitor-processTradeallocationGroupComplete:"><st=
rong>processTradeallocationGroupComplete:</strong></h4>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Retrieve all the trades from the <strong>TradeRequestMonitorAggregatorMe=
ssage</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"0eecd220-60e0-4f94-a69=
1-b02c54adcd7a">Total all the proceeds in the list and add them a new field=
 called totalProceeds</span></p></li>
<li>
<p>Send a new <strong>TradeAllocationGroupCompleteMessage</strong> kafka me=
ssage containing the above list and total proceeds to a new kafka topic <st=
rong><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"92d35235-a2f4-42f7-9=
a14-42c001fbf30b">trade_allocation_group_complete</span></strong><span clas=
s=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"92d35235-a2f4-42f7-9a14-42c001fbf30=
b">. </span></p></li>
</ol>
<p>4. Save the details of the group status and update the total proceeds co=
lumn.</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapp=
er confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image=
 image-center" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"caf653209fd5ebe5b1f8fe=
c6477c1de7551da7967ff6412d3982f63c743fd302" data-image-src=3D"https://purpl=
egroup3.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/3075866628/image-20230512-1=
14216.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1683891828117&amp;cacheVersion=
=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"471" data-width=3D"728" data-unresolved-c=
omment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"3094216709" data-linked-resou=
rce-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-reso=
urce-default-alias=3D"image-20230512-114216.png" data-base-url=3D"https://p=
urplegroup3.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/=
png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"3075866628" data-linked-resource-=
container-version=3D"34" data-media-id=3D"246fe17a-eff3-443e-a7f5-5b04c3528=
ee9" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"303"></span>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"0ea220b5-0e78-4c82-81e=
b-4707de932660">This is the new end state right?</span></p><span class=3D"c=
onfluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper"><img class=3D"conflue=
nce-embedded-image image-center" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"1e228cb13c7fcf1bb9=
d1995540584114e40cd5dbef8b1e2663b0b895fd33692a" data-image-src=3D"https://p=
urplegroup3.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/3075866628/image-202306=
09-092839.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1686302923677&amp;cacheVer=
sion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"655" data-width=3D"760" data-unresolv=
ed-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"3117875216" data-linked-r=
esource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-=
resource-default-alias=3D"image-20230609-092839.png" data-base-url=3D"https=
://purplegroup3.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"im=
age/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"3075866628" data-linked-resou=
rce-container-version=3D"34" data-media-id=3D"b7db9e2a-32b1-4e23-83c4-12e41=
8cf405c" data-media-type=3D"file" width=3D"468" height=3D"403"></span>
<p>API methods:</p>
<h4 id=3D"TradeAllocationsMonitor-GETmethods:">GET methods:</h4>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Query status of group by <code>group id</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>Query by <code>tradeallocationid</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>Query by <code>transactionid</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>CRUD methods via spring data rest to alter and query all tables</p></li>
<li>
<p>An API method to reconstruct the <strong>TradeAllocationGroupCompleteMes=
sage</strong> from the Mongodb and resending to the kafka topic.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>Save the static data below to a table and create an API method to return=
 a list of status ids with descriptions:</p>
<p><strong>AllocationStatusId details</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"22=
365d3a-9f3e-418e-9935-4beed36624c4" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p style=3D"text-align: center;"><strong>AllocationStatusID</strong></p></t=
h>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p style=3D"text-align: center;"><strong>Description</strong></p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
